STEP 3: ADD SOURCE CODE
================================================================

Copy the consolidated source code into the respective files.

IMPORTANT:

Do not put all Java classes into one physical Java file.

Each public Java class must be saved in its own file.

Use the filename delimiters in the consolidated source document
to identify where each class belongs.

Save YAML configurations under src/main/resources.

Save test classes under src/test/java.


STEP 4: CONFIGURE LOCAL ENVIRONMENT
================================================================

Open terminal in the project directory.

Linux / macOS:

export SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=local

export JWT_ISSUER_URI=https://your-test-identity-provider

export INVESTMENT_API_URL=http://localhost:9090

export GPN_CLAIM=userGpn

Windows PowerShell:

$env:SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE="local"

$env:JWT_ISSUER_URI="https://your-test-identity-provider"

$env:INVESTMENT_API_URL="http://localhost:9090"

$env:GPN_CLAIM="userGpn"

Replace these values with your actual local environment settings.

JWT_ISSUER_URI:
Issuer URL of the identity provider.

INVESTMENT_API_URL:
Base URL of the investment API.

GPN_CLAIM:
JWT claim containing the user's GPN.

Do not hardcode authentication tokens in application.yml.


STEP 5: CONFIGURE EXTERNAL API
================================================================

Configure application-local.yml:

app:
  investment-api:
    base-url: http://localhost:9090
    insights-path: /api/investment/insights
    connect-timeout: 5000
    read-timeout: 15000

The external API should accept:

HTTP METHOD:
POST

ENDPOINT:
/api/investment/insights

HEADERS:

Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>

x_user_gpn: <USER_GPN>

Content-Type: application/json

EXPECTED REQUEST BODY:

{
  "filter": {
    "insightType": "ASSET_ALLOCATION",
    "holdingsFlag": true
  }
}

The actual request structure must match your external
investment API contract.


